select public.prepify_load_bank('Computer Science', 5, $j$[["Which best describes the difference between Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML)?",["They are the same technology with different names","AI is a branch of ML","ML is a subset of AI that lets computers learn from data without explicit programming","ML is hardware while AI is software"],"C",3,0,"836bddb665ea"],["Which pair names the two main types of Machine Learning?",["Deep learning and neural networks","Supervised and unsupervised learning","Reinforcement and transfer learning","Predictive and descriptive learning"],"B",1,0,"4cb6b8115663"],["In supervised machine learning, what is the main role of labelled data?",["To find hidden patterns without categories","To train the algorithm with known inputs and their correct outputs","To remove irrelevant features","To group similar points into clusters"],"B",3,0,"7bb84c4a9f98"],["A data scientist's dataset has no predefined labels, and the algorithm must find hidden patterns and group similar points. This approach is:",["Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Unsupervised learning","Deep learning"],"C",3,1,"3cfea4ba3e96"],["How is Computer Vision related to AI?",["It is completely separate from AI","It is a field of AI that extracts meaningful information from images and videos","It only works with text","It needs no data or algorithms"],"B",3,0,"ed44c8bb7316"],["The technology that lets computers understand, interpret and respond to human language in spoken and written form is:",["Computer vision","Speech recognition","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Expert systems"],"C",1,0,"3fdfe82ee960"],["Which statement correctly distinguishes speech recognition from Natural Language Processing?",["Speech recognition turns spoken words into text, while NLP understands and processes language","They are identical","NLP only works with images","Speech recognition is part of computer vision"],"A",3,0,"d3a8d738a170"],["An AI medical assistant uses stored expert knowledge, rules and reasoning to analyze symptoms and suggest solutions. What type of AI system is this?",["A storage system that only saves information","A system that replaces all human experts","An expert system that reasons with expert knowledge to solve complex problems","A basic calculation program"],"C",3,1,"266cc0d62b70"],["What is the first stage in developing an expert system?",["Applying rules to find solutions","Building a knowledge base by gathering information from experts","Giving solutions to end users","Asking users to fill a questionnaire"],"B",3,0,"a16968ce5a9c"],["Which correctly distinguishes a chatbot from a virtual assistant?",["A chatbot uses only text and a virtual assistant only voice","A chatbot answers website visitors' questions, while virtual assistants like Siri perform many tasks on devices","Chatbots are not based on AI","They are identical"],"B",3,0,"78ba020a9e48"],["What is the main purpose of cloud computing?",["To store data only on local computers","To deliver computing services such as servers, storage, databases and software over the Internet","To replace all physical computers","To remove the need for the Internet"],"B",1,0,"f2139344bb96"],["Which cloud model has resources owned, operated and maintained by a service provider and delivered over the Internet to many users?",["Private cloud","Public cloud","Hybrid cloud","Community cloud"],"B",3,0,"a2b377aef259"],["Which statement correctly distinguishes a private cloud from a public cloud?",["A private cloud belongs to a provider and a public cloud to one organization","A private cloud is dedicated to one organization with full control, while a public cloud serves many organizations over the Internet","A private cloud is cheaper in all cases","A private cloud needs no infrastructure"],"B",3,0,"782d64a268ee"],["In AI in education, which of these is NOT a benefit?",["Adapting to each student's learning needs","Grading assignments and essays","Replacing all human teachers","Scheduling courses and timetables"],"C",3,0,"4f8d8da1c927"],["Which ethical issues are specifically associated with ChatGPT?",["It cannot understand any language","It causes physical harm","Cheating, plagiarism, misinformation, bias and data privacy","It is only for entertainment"],"C",3,0,"cef99cc53130"],["Which correctly identifies a limitation of AI algorithms?",["They are always 100% accurate","They never make errors","They can produce wrong results, and how they reach decisions is often not transparent","They follow fixed formulas that guarantee correct results"],"C",3,0,"b11964f84d63"],["What is a hybrid cloud?",["A cloud that only stores data","A cloud owned equally by many organizations","A combination of public and private clouds that can share data and applications","A cloud that does not use the Internet"],"C",3,0,"671fd6e17480"],["Which describes a possible negative impact of AI-based automation?",["It creates unlimited jobs in every sector","It can cause job losses in areas such as manufacturing, business and healthcare","It has no effect on employment","It affects only technology jobs"],"B",3,0,"2c3e6ea0a949"],["A hospital's AI analyzes X-rays and MRI scans to spot early cancer after being trained on thousands of images already labelled by doctors. Which type of machine learning is this?",["Unsupervised learning","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Clustering"],"B",5,1,"7475c7f494c9"],["A bank's AI predicts loan defaulters from income, debt, credit history, age, gender and mobile number. Which data should be removed from the model to keep it fair and relevant?",["Monthly income and credit history","Monthly income and debt","Age, mobile number and gender","Debt and credit history"],"C",5,1,"67368e3cbf4b"],["The steps are: collect training data, create an algorithm, learning process, create a training model, predict results. This sequence is:",["Building an expert system","The machine learning process","Deploying cloud computing","The NLP workflow"],"B",3,1,"382dc0bccbfc"],["A school's AI adapts lessons to each student, helps teachers grade work and helps administrators schedule courses. This is AI applied in:",["Healthcare","Gaming","Education","Defence"],"C",1,1,"e56434cbf009"],["An e-commerce website runs a program that answers customer questions instantly through text, 24/7. This is an example of a:",["Expert system","Chatbot","Virtual assistant","Computer vision system"],"B",3,1,"baef3d64379c"],["Model X shares resources with many organizations over the Internet; Model Y is dedicated to one organization; Model Z combines both. What are X, Y and Z?",["X private, Y public, Z hybrid","X public, Y private, Z hybrid","X hybrid, Y public, Z private","X private, Y hybrid, Z public"],"B",5,1,"54b2fe32cf99"],["A university worries that students use ChatGPT to write essays, harming learning and fair assessment. Which ethical issues are relevant?",["Only data privacy","Cheating, plagiarism and a negative impact on teaching and learning","Only security risks","Only bias"],"B",3,1,"c7008c197a87"],["A farmer uses AI drones to monitor crops, detect insect attacks and spray pesticides, and cameras with computer vision to check livestock health. This is AI applied in:",["Healthcare","Business","Agriculture","Defence"],"C",1,1,"427ae7ba332a"],["An AI tool corrects spelling and grammar, helps improve writing, but is not 100% accurate and cannot replace manual proofreading. Which tool is it?",["ChatGPT","Lovo AI","Grammarly","A virtual assistant"],"C",3,1,"2ca51f311801"],["A company builds AI for self-driving cars that uses sensors, cameras and radar to travel without a driver. Which field of AI is mainly applied?",["Natural Language Processing","Expert systems","Computer vision","Speech recognition"],"C",3,1,"07b93739a48b"],["A text-to-speech AI tool offers about 500 voices in over 100 languages, and its developers must handle personal data carefully and avoid biased training data. Which tool is this?",["ChatGPT","Grammarly","Lovo AI","Google Assistant"],"C",3,1,"25cf4945936c"],["A military uses AI to detect cyber threats, find suspicious activity, prevent unauthorized access and train soldiers in simulated wars. This is AI applied in:",["Healthcare","Education","Business","Defence"],"D",1,1,"938419e9a43b"],["A company keeps sensitive records on its own private servers but uses a public provider's servers for its website. This is a:",["public cloud","private cloud","hybrid cloud","community cloud"],"C",3,1,"671fd6e17480"],["An AI model learns to recognise cats after being trained on thousands of photos already labelled \"cat\" or \"not cat\". This is:",["unsupervised learning","supervised learning","reinforcement learning","rule-based programming"],"B",3,1,"7475c7f494c9"],["A bank website has a program that answers customers' typed questions at any hour. This is a:",["chatbot","expert system","computer virus","spreadsheet"],"A",1,1,"baef3d64379c"],["Google Drive and Dropbox, which anyone can sign up for over the Internet, are examples of:",["private cloud","public cloud","hybrid cloud","local storage"],"B",3,0,"a2b377aef259"],["Which is a limitation of AI systems?",["They are always 100% accurate","They can give wrong results and their decisions are hard to explain","They never need data","They cannot run on computers"],"B",3,0,"b11964f84d63"],["A factory replaces many workers with AI-controlled robots. Which negative impact of AI does this show?",["Job losses","Better medical diagnosis","Faster translation","Fewer road accidents"],"A",3,1,"2c3e6ea0a949"],["Building an expert system begins with:",["gathering knowledge from human experts into a knowledge base","selling the software","testing it with users","printing the results"],"A",3,0,"a16968ce5a9c"],["Turning spoken words into written text is called:",["speech recognition","computer vision","data mining","encryption"],"A",1,0,"d3a8d738a170"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('Computer Science', 6, $j$[["When creating a \"strong and unique password,\" what specific mix is recommended?",["Capital and lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters.","Only your name followed by your birth year.","Just a long list of numbers that are easy to remember.","The name of your favorite sports team and city."],"A",3,0,"a0a8c93b40ce"],["Why is it important to backup data in a \"safe place\" like an external drive or the cloud?",["To make sure other people can see your files easily.","To ensure you would not lose your important data if your computer gets stolen or damaged.","To clear space on the computer so it can play games faster.","To follow government rules about internet usage."],"B",3,0,"2a73a842f340"],["What is the specific misleading technique used by scammers during a phishing attack?",["Using a program to slow down your internet speed.","Scammers pretend to be official and try to trick you.","Physically stealing the external hard drive from your home.","Sending unsolicited and irrelevant messages via email."],"B",3,0,"9b467f5894b1"],["Public Wi-Fi networks are generally avoided for private tasks because they are:",["Too expensive to use for long periods.","More susceptible to hackers.","Not allowed to open banking websites.","Only available in large city centers."],"B",3,0,"52d17ad2e44a"],["To ensure the safety of your system from malware, what is the rule for downloading files?",["Download apps, programs, and files only from reliable websites.","Download only from websites that do not require any login details.","Open every attachment in emails to check for potential updates.","Only download files when your antivirus software is turned off."],"A",3,0,"0ce85b198827"],["Regarding physical security, what action should you take for your workspace?",["Keep your computer screen visible to everyone in the room.","Lock your computer when you are away from it.","Avoid using any passwords for your social media accounts.","Share your home address on all digital platforms for verification."],"B",3,0,"418029ea4075"],["Ethical use of software requires a user to avoid:",["Updating the software to the latest version.","Malicious purposes, such as hacking, spreading malware, or cyberbullying.","Using software for educational or business tasks.","Changing the privacy settings of the software."],"B",3,1,"eb0359c88ad1"],["\"Protection of Individual Rights\" in the digital age means:",["Everyone has the right to use any software for free.","Safeguarding a person's personal information, freedom, and privacy.","Preventing the government from ever seeing your online activities.","Allowing people to copy anyone’s work without permission."],"B",3,0,"069e091eae21"],["What mental health conditions are associated with the \"harmful effect\" of digital addiction?",["Anxiety, depression, and social isolation.","Increased focus and better memory.","Improved social skills and physical health.","A better understanding of computer hardware."],"A",3,0,"aef766fe5f69"],["Which general term describes any software that is specifically created with the intent to harm, exploit, or disrupt a computer network?",["Phishing","Malware","Hacking","Cookies"],"B",3,0,"5e0ba7ac93f9"],["If a cybercriminal uses fake emails or websites to trick individuals into revealing sensitive information, what is this specific deceptive method called?",["Malware","Phishing","Hacking","Pharming"],"B",3,1,"575faab66260"],["What is the term used for unsolicited, irrelevant, or inappropriate messages sent over the internet?",["Spyware","Pharming","Spam","Hacking"],"C",3,0,"f1a1e5677048"],["What specific tool should be used to encrypt a connection if necessary when using public Wi-Fi?",["Browser cookies","Virtual private network (VPN)","Antivirus program","Public hotspot"],"B",3,0,"616cf5feafdd"],["A software tracking your online activities and sending the data to advertisers without your knowledge or consent is called:",["Spam","Phishing","Spyware","Pharming"],"C",3,0,"023708328fc0"],["When a computer system or network faces unauthorized access or manipulation, it is called:",["Hacking","Phishing","Malware","Spyware"],"A",3,0,"222a1b56fd6f"],["When a person is targeted by deceptive schemes that are explicitly designed to trick people for financial gain or personal information, what is it called?",["Cookies","Scam","Pharming","Software Piracy"],"B",3,0,"b83ef8716b93"],["If someone engages in the unauthorized copying, distribution, or use of software without proper licensing, which term defines this act?",["Freeware","Shareware","Software Piracy","Cookies"],"C",3,0,"c06ee09ccecc"],["What term describes the small text files stored on a user's device, containing information about their interactions with a website?",["Shareware","Scam","Freeware","Cookies"],"D",3,1,"e920e696c40a"],["What specific threat is carried out by redirecting website traffic to a fake site without the user's knowledge?",["Cookies","Scam","Shareware","Pharming"],"D",3,1,"01086ff5cc44"],["If a user downloads Mozilla Firefox, which is a free web browser, what type of software are they using?",["Shareware","Freeware","Software Piracy","Scam"],"B",3,1,"486744774259"],["If an organization adopts the Linux operating system because its source code can be openly viewed, modified, and distributed by anyone, what type of software are they utilizing?",["Shareware","Open Source","Freeware","Tradeoff"],"B",3,1,"fe0e54f3372d"],["Using complex passwords or encryption to protect your data is a practical example of:",["Information Privacy","System Security","Tradeoff","Access Control"],"A",3,0,"e2ce7c1c4a6c"],["Firewalls, encryption, antivirus software, and access control are all classified as core examples of:",["Information Privacy","System Security","Open Source","Tradeoffs"],"B",3,0,"976275ff3820"],["Online platforms like Facebook, WhatsApp, and Instagram are explicitly designed to facilitate the exchange of:",["Fake news and disinformation","Deceptive schemes and updates","Ideas, interests, and personal updates","Public discourse and restrictions"],"C",3,0,"26460ab8d978"],["The Apple logo on iPhones and MacBooks is a direct, practical example of which legal tool?",["Patent","Copyright","Trademark","Disinformation"],"C",3,0,"35000a8480bd"],["When an author writes a book and automatically holds the legal right that prevents others from reproducing or distributing the work without permission, they are exercising a:",["Patent","Copyright","Trademark","Tradeoff"],"B",3,0,"dc3532e5092a"],["Ensuring that no one can copy or use someone else's work (such as books, music, or software) without permission is the primary function of:",["Protection of Individual Rights","Intellectual Property Ownership","Prevention of Unauthorized Use","Software Copyright"],"B",3,0,"4828b4b20012"],["While social media and messaging apps make communication fast and easy, which tools specifically simplify finding information?",["Secure digital payments","Search engines like Google","Automation and technology","Software development"],"B",3,1,"9528066dde49"],["Which specific issue is facilitated by social media platforms when individuals are harassed, threatened, or humiliated online?",["Security breach","Cyberbullying","Disinformation","Tradeoff"],"B",3,0,"02f8da105c9d"],["Fake news on social networking platforms specifically refers to false or misleading information that is presented as:",["Conspiracy theories","Factual news","Security breaches","Analytical data"],"B",3,0,"c838a495a0e3"],["One article is deliberately created to make people believe something false; another wrong report is shared without any intent to harm. Which option explains the difference?",["Disinformation is always political","Disinformation involves intentional deception, while fake news may be false without deliberate intent to harm","Fake news spreads only on social media","Both terms mean exactly the same"],"B",5,1,"74cad95e587f"],["A website collects personal details from children. What does a children's online privacy law specifically control?",["Every type of cyber attack on all users","The online collection of personal information from children under 13","Hacking of government systems","Security standards for all business networks"],"B",3,1,"ee368aa5aaf8"],["A user finds that unknown software is secretly monitoring activity and collecting personal information without permission. Which malware is responsible?",["A virus that attaches itself to programs","Ransomware that locks data for payment","Spyware that secretly gathers information","A Trojan horse disguised as a useful program"],"C",3,1,"afc522fbfe4d"],["A student sees that a website's address begins with HTTPS instead of HTTP. What does this mainly indicate?",["The site is faster than every HTTP site","Communication with the site is protected by encryption","The site is government approved","The site has no adverts or harmful content"],"B",3,1,"eac66556acff"],["A Canadian company collects and uses customers' personal information. Which law sets the rules for protecting this information in the private sector?",["A cybersecurity law covering all internet crime","The Telecommunications Act","The Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA)","A computer crimes act about illegal access"],"C",3,1,"4c03f025a16d"],["What security feature does HTTPS provide?",["Faster internet speed","Encryption of communication between user and server","Automatic blocking of all viruses","Removal of website adverts"],"B",1,0,"d1f47c090efd"],["A user types the correct address of a banking website but is secretly redirected to a fake site. Which attack is this?",["Phishing, using fake messages to steal information","Pharming, redirecting users to fraudulent websites","Spyware, monitoring the user secretly","Spam, sending unwanted messages"],"B",5,1,"05cbeae974a8"],["A user cannot use online resources because their area lacks internet facilities and technology. This situation represents the:",["Cybercrime","Digital divide","Data privacy","Digital footprint"],"B",3,1,"efa6b2ba40ce"],["A company invents a new device and wants the legal right to stop others making or selling it for a limited time. Which protection should it apply for?",["Trademark","Copyright","Patent","Trade secret"],"C",3,1,"c7e03ecdcf37"],["What is the main function of cookies on websites?",["To delete browsing history","To store small text files about a user's interactions with the site","To encrypt all transmitted data","To block unauthorized access"],"B",3,0,"80a8d2b41ea0"],["A user is creating a password for an online account. Which practice is most secure?",["Only small letters, to remember it easily","Personal details such as name and birth date","A mix of uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers and symbols","Common dictionary words"],"C",1,1,"2eea4312f915"],["A government law allows authorities to monitor communication channels under specific conditions and controls access to communication records. Which area does it mainly address?",["Children's online activity","Interception of telecommunications and access to communication data","Prevention of computer viruses","Business data storage"],"B",3,1,"e9f4c974f4fb"],["A company wants to improve system security while protecting user privacy. Which statement best explains the relationship?",["Security and privacy are unrelated","Stronger privacy protection can need controls that affect convenience and usability","Better security always reduces privacy","Privacy removes the need for security"],"B",5,0,"ea8e9b1ee3d5"],["One program can be used free forever; another can be used free only for a limited trial. What is the difference?",["Freeware is always open source","Freeware is free permanently, while shareware is usually a limited trial","Shareware is always more secure","Freeware needs payment"],"B",3,0,"dc4a881638dd"],["A new computing innovation improves communication, automates tasks and increases efficiency. Which is NOT one of its benefits?",["Improved productivity","Automated repetitive work","Completely removing all cybersecurity threats","Better communication"],"C",3,0,"0e09d6abfb88"],["A student searches websites, posts comments and uploads pictures. The trail of information these activities create is the:",["Storage capacity of the computer","Digital footprint","Number of devices owned","Internet speed"],"B",1,1,"21da561b6770"],["Which practice shows responsible software use?",["Using illegally modified software to avoid payment","Sharing one licensed copy with unlimited users","Following software licences and respecting copyright","Turning off security software to speed up"],"C",3,0,"96edbe61ea1c"],["A school network administrator wants to protect computers by monitoring and controlling network connections. Which tool should be used?",["Antivirus that only removes infected files","A firewall that controls incoming and outgoing traffic","A password generator","Backup software"],"B",3,1,"031b5aa84505"],["Aisha gets an email that looks like it is from her bank, asking her to click a link and verify her account; the sender's address is slightly different from the bank's. What threat is this?",["Phishing","Pharming","Spyware","Ransomware"],"A",3,1,"077f5db8cb8a"],["A company develops new software and automatically holds the right to control how it is copied and distributed. Which protection applies?",["Patent","Trademark","Copyright","Trade secret"],"C",3,1,"9b4f0646c4ba"],["Ali posts his address, phone number and daily schedule on social media and uses the same password for every account. Which safety practice is he violating?",["He is being too social","He overshares personal information and uses weak password practices","He should post more to be safe","Reusing one password is recommended"],"B",3,1,"21f1bf6295bb"],["A person gains unauthorized access to a company's database and steals customers' credit card details. What is this called?",["Spam","Phishing","Hacking","Pharming"],"C",1,1,"6e6c7120060a"],["Fatima copies her important files to an external drive and cloud storage in case her laptop is stolen or damaged. Which security measure is this?",["Strong passwords","A firewall","Backing up data","Updating software"],"C",1,1,"a35f594e5068"],["A site shows \"Your connection is not secure\" beside the URL just as users are about to enter card details. What should they do?",["Continue, it is probably a mistake","Avoid entering sensitive information and leave the site","Ignore the warning","Refresh until it disappears"],"B",3,1,"fe66c37722c1"],["Ahmed's antivirus warns that a file from an untrusted site contains a virus, but he opens it anyway. What is the most likely result?",["His computer runs faster","His computer may be infected with malware","The file becomes safe","His antivirus stops working"],"B",3,1,"275b8895f9d7"],["A rural school has limited internet, while a city school has fast connections and the latest computers, so rural students cannot use online resources well. This illustrates the:",["Phishing","Digital divide","Cyberbullying","Malware"],"B",3,1,"77b3db90edf1"],["Zara uses a coffee shop's public Wi-Fi for online banking and sees suspicious account activity the next day. What was the risk?",["Sensitive transactions over public Wi-Fi can be intercepted by hackers","Coffee shop Wi-Fi is always secure","Banking must be done on desktops only","She needed a shorter password"],"A",3,1,"51cc0e7ff8bc"],["A completely false story that a celebrity has died spreads quickly online; its creator made it to get more views and traffic. This is an example of:",["Disinformation","Factual reporting","Educational content","Scientific research"],"A",3,1,"d08abe69895b"],["Hassan finds paid software offered free on an unofficial website and wants to download it to save money. What should he consider?",["Free downloads from unofficial sources often contain malware","All free software is safe","Unofficial downloads are always legal","Price is the only factor"],"A",3,1,"386a4f403cfb"],["Sarah posted a holiday photo showing her house number and street while she was away, and her home was broken into a week later. What could have prevented this?",["Strong passwords","Privacy settings and not sharing location details publicly","Antivirus software","Backing up her data"],"B",3,1,"ee5ae57321e1"],["Bilal receives a message claiming he has won a prize and must enter his bank PIN on a link. This is an example of:",["phishing","a firewall","a backup","a cookie"],"A",1,1,"077f5db8cb8a"],["A user types the correct web address of a shopping site but is secretly sent to a fake copy of it. This attack is:",["phishing","pharming","spam","a backup"],"B",5,0,"05cbeae974a8"],["Small text files that a website stores on your device to remember your preferences are called:",["viruses","cookies","patches","firewalls"],"B",1,0,"e920e696c40a"],["Software that secretly records a user's online activity and sends it to others without permission is:",["freeware","spyware","a firewall","a browser"],"B",3,0,"023708328fc0"],["An inventor wants the legal right to stop others copying her new machine for a number of years. She should apply for a:",["trademark","copyright","patent","licence to drive"],"C",3,1,"c7e03ecdcf37"],["The golden \"M\" logo of a fast-food chain is protected by a:",["patent","copyright","trademark","firewall"],"C",3,0,"35000a8480bd"],["Which tool monitors and controls the traffic entering and leaving a school network?",["A firewall","A printer driver","A spreadsheet","A cookie"],"A",3,0,"031b5aa84505"],["Viruses, worms and trojan horses all belong to the general category of:",["malware","cookies","freeware","hardware"],"A",1,0,"5e0ba7ac93f9"],["Hamza keeps copies of his project files on a USB drive and in cloud storage in case his computer fails. This is:",["backing up data","hacking","pharming","encryption"],"A",1,1,"a35f594e5068"],["Someone breaks into a school's computer system without permission and changes students' marks. This is:",["hacking","spam","a backup","a trademark"],"A",3,1,"6e6c7120060a"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
